  "evidence": "Closes N8N-21534\n\nFixed wildcard domain matching in isDomainAllowed: '*.example.com' used endsWith('example.com') without a dot boundary, so lookalikes like evilexample.com were allowed. It now requires the '.example.com' suffix. Added tests for lookalike hosts and the bare domain.\n\n### What changed\n- `packages/workflow/src/utils.ts`\n- `packages/workflow/test/utils.test.ts`\n\n### What ran\n- The agent ran tests 1 time(s): acdc-test test/utils.test.ts passed (77 of 77). acdc-lint failed to run (tsgolint executable not found). acdc-typecheck printed no output, so I have no result from it.\n- After the agent, the executor ran: tests fail, type check passes, lint passes\n- **The agent said the tests pass; the executor's run says they do not.**\n\n### Risks that remain\n- Change risk: medium (10% chance of a revert or follow-up fix, from n8n's history)\n- Behavior change: '*.example.com' no longer matches the bare 'example.com'; users relying on that must list the apex domain explicitly.\n- Allowed-domain entries are not lowercased, so mixed-case entries won't match (existing behavior, not changed).\n- Lint and typecheck did not produce a usable result.\n\n### Where a person decides\n- Autonomy level: **agent reviewed**\n- category bugfix: at most agent_reviewed\n",
